1
00:00:06,634 --> 00:00:08,434
Yomogi Kindergarten

2
00:00:09,374 --> 00:00:10,434
Yes!

3
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:13,844
Kobato. Kobato!

4
00:00:13,844 --> 00:00:14,844
Yes?

5
00:00:14,844 --> 00:00:17,274
Can you read this?

6
00:00:20,284 --> 00:00:20,654
Firefly's Light
Written by Sotaro Mori Drawings by Naoko Niimura

7
00:00:20,654 --> 00:00:22,814
Firefly's Light
Written by Sotaro Mori Drawings by Naoko Niimura
Firefly's Light...

8
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:24,284
Firefly's Light
Written by Sotaro Mori Drawings by Naoko Niimura

9
00:00:24,654 --> 00:00:26,454
Please?! Read it for us!

10
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:27,514
Huh?

11
00:00:27,654 --> 00:00:30,164
Kobato, don't tell us you can't read!

12
00:00:30,164 --> 00:00:31,714
What?!

13
00:00:32,194 --> 00:00:34,164
Of course I can read!

14
00:00:39,634 --> 00:00:42,774
Kobato.

15
00:00:42,774 --> 00:00:45,604
Kobato.
What should I do?

16
00:00:45,604 --> 00:00:50,014
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

17
00:00:50,914 --> 00:00:54,214
Are always such a challenge

18
00:00:54,214 --> 00:00:56,984
I want to laugh when I'm happy

19
00:00:56,984 --> 00:01:01,284
And sing whenever I want

20
00:01:01,854 --> 00:01:04,294
Is all

21
00:01:05,594 --> 00:01:09,964
They say my dreams will come true someday

22
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:13,674
But when will "someday" come?

23
00:01:13,674 --> 00:01:17,164
I can't wait forever

24
00:01:17,304 --> 00:01:23,074
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

25
00:01:23,074 --> 00:01:28,284
And let the light gather around me

26
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:31,124
Where is it?

27
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:34,454
Please tell me what I can do

28
00:01:34,454 --> 00:01:37,294
I make the most of getting hurt

29
00:01:37,294 --> 00:01:40,194
And run with all my might

30
00:01:40,194 --> 00:01:44,164
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

31
00:01:44,164 --> 00:01:47,204
And start crying

32
00:01:47,204 --> 00:01:51,234
I surprise myself

33
00:01:51,704 --> 00:01:55,874
In how much I believe in tomorrow

34
00:02:05,524 --> 00:02:05,754
And when night fell, all became dark.

35
00:02:05,754 --> 00:02:09,594
...Firefly Promise.
And when night fell, all became dark.

36
00:02:09,594 --> 00:02:10,264
...Firefly Promise.

37
00:02:10,264 --> 00:02:11,224
...Firefly Promise.
Even the moon was taking a rest.

38
00:02:11,224 --> 00:02:14,394
Even the moon was taking a rest.

39
00:02:16,034 --> 00:02:18,394
Nothing is visible...

40
00:02:19,534 --> 00:02:21,004
...but it is now visible.

41
00:02:22,704 --> 00:02:25,374
Kobato, you skipped pages again!

42
00:02:25,374 --> 00:02:26,394
What?!

43
00:02:26,504 --> 00:02:30,204
Oh, I'm sorry. Um, Um... Agh!

44
00:02:31,744 --> 00:02:33,384
Clumsy, as usual.

45
00:02:33,384 --> 00:02:34,574
Huh?!

46
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:39,044
Hang in there Kobato!

47
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,444
Yes!

48
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:44,214
Good grief... Did she mess up again?

49
00:02:53,974 --> 00:02:56,134
Yomogi Kindergarten, may I help you?

50
00:02:57,944 --> 00:03:00,434
I thought I made it clear that the answer is "no".

51
00:03:02,674 --> 00:03:05,474
Kindergarten is in session. Goodbye.

52
00:03:11,784 --> 00:03:13,694
Kobato fell down again!

53
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,084
Your nose is all red!

54
00:03:15,854 --> 00:03:18,194
I can't believe you fell again!

55
00:03:18,764 --> 00:03:20,134
Dobato! It's not time to be fooling around.

56
00:03:20,134 --> 00:03:22,064
Do - Ba - To -
Dobato! It's not time to be fooling around.

57
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:22,664
Do - Ba - To -
There are issues at stake!

58
00:03:22,664 --> 00:03:23,994
There are issues at stake!

59
00:03:25,434 --> 00:03:27,474
Bye-bye Kobato!

60
00:03:27,474 --> 00:03:29,194
Yes, bye-bye.

61
00:03:30,174 --> 00:03:31,764
Kobato, Kobato!

62
00:03:32,174 --> 00:03:33,974
What is it, Marina?

63
00:03:34,174 --> 00:03:37,244
Good luck in learning to read
the picture book well.

64
00:03:37,244 --> 00:03:39,514
Yes, I'll do my best.

65
00:03:39,784 --> 00:03:43,214
You'll be okay. I'm sure you'll
eventually get good at it.

66
00:03:43,524 --> 00:03:44,714
Yes!

67
00:04:00,304 --> 00:04:01,464
Um...

68
00:04:02,374 --> 00:04:06,204
I'd like to practice so I can
make everyone happy.

69
00:04:06,204 --> 00:04:08,274
May I borrow this?

70
00:04:08,274 --> 00:04:11,274
Oh, uh... By all means.

71
00:04:11,844 --> 00:04:14,214
I'm going to do my best so I can read better!

72
00:04:14,484 --> 00:04:16,454
Mhm. Good luck with that.

73
00:04:17,254 --> 00:04:18,344
Yes ma'am!

74
00:04:21,024 --> 00:04:26,554
Firefly had been living all
alone for a long, long time.

75
00:04:26,764 --> 00:04:32,534
It had been so long that Firefly had
completely forgotten that he was a firefly.

76
00:04:34,134 --> 00:04:36,624
It must be lonely being alone.

77
00:04:37,274 --> 00:04:38,604
Yeah, I guess.

78
00:04:38,804 --> 00:04:45,874
I sort of recall something wonderful
happening on pitch dark nights like tonight.

79
00:04:45,944 --> 00:04:47,074
Hey.

80
00:04:49,784 --> 00:04:52,084
Did you want to talk to me?

81
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:54,854
Yeah. Would you stop that?

82
00:04:56,424 --> 00:04:58,954
I'm asking you to quit reading that book.

83
00:04:59,394 --> 00:05:01,594
Um... why is that?

84
00:05:03,964 --> 00:05:06,124
Not a very nice type, is he?

85
00:05:09,734 --> 00:05:11,204
What is it?

86
00:05:11,574 --> 00:05:12,974
It's that guy again.

87
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:18,604
You're right.

88
00:05:18,684 --> 00:05:19,944
What's up with him?

89
00:05:20,314 --> 00:05:22,374
He seems totally different now.

90
00:05:23,654 --> 00:05:26,484
I wonder if he's got something troubling him.

91
00:05:30,124 --> 00:05:31,594
Excuse me!

92
00:05:33,294 --> 00:05:35,054
Do you not have a place to live?!

93
00:05:35,764 --> 00:05:37,004
How'd she come up with that?!

94
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:41,034
In fact, until just the other day, I too was
homeless and lived in the park too.

95
00:05:41,034 --> 00:05:46,304
Then, thanks to Ms. Sayaka and Ms. Chisato,
I now get to sleep in a fluffy futon!

96
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:48,604
Futon mattresses are nice!

97
00:05:49,744 --> 00:05:52,874
If it's okay with you, why not come to my home?

98
00:05:53,814 --> 00:05:56,684
I don't plan to be taken in
by a complete stranger!

99
00:05:56,854 --> 00:06:00,344
I'm Kobato Hanato! And this is Ioryogi-san!

100
00:06:07,964 --> 00:06:09,454
I've had enough of you.

101
00:06:12,234 --> 00:06:13,394
Um...

102
00:06:14,904 --> 00:06:17,604
I wonder why he got angry with me.

103
00:06:20,914 --> 00:06:25,784
Firefly saw a small pretty light in the distance.

104
00:06:25,784 --> 00:06:27,974
Wondering what it was, he went closer...

105
00:06:33,824 --> 00:06:35,914
I am clumsy, just like he said.

106
00:06:44,164 --> 00:06:46,264
I'll do better tomorrow, for sure!

107
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:53,814
I slept in, again!

108
00:06:53,814 --> 00:06:56,214
You're clumsy, whatever you do.

109
00:06:56,544 --> 00:06:59,774
If you're late, Fujimoto will
be on your case again!

110
00:07:03,414 --> 00:07:04,944
Wow! That's fast!

111
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:17,054
What?

112
00:07:17,204 --> 00:07:19,894
Ah? What is it, little girl?

113
00:07:19,964 --> 00:07:24,144
Good morning! May I help you?

114
00:07:24,144 --> 00:07:25,194
Huh?

115
00:07:25,504 --> 00:07:29,004
We're here to collect debt owed to us!

116
00:07:29,144 --> 00:07:30,974
Huh? Debt?

117
00:07:31,914 --> 00:07:34,004
Doesn't look very good.

118
00:07:34,314 --> 00:07:39,154
Go on, eat it! I like little kids.

119
00:07:39,254 --> 00:07:40,774
Come on!

120
00:07:42,094 --> 00:07:43,494
Please stop that!

121
00:07:44,294 --> 00:07:45,784
What do you think you're doing?!

122
00:07:51,434 --> 00:07:55,424
You bump into me, and not
even a simple "I'm sorry"?

123
00:07:55,804 --> 00:07:57,964
Well? Well?!

124
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:08,384
What the hell?! Get your hands off of me!

125
00:08:08,584 --> 00:08:10,344
Don't you touch the kids!

126
00:08:11,024 --> 00:08:12,624
Fujimoto!

127
00:08:12,624 --> 00:08:14,024
Damn you!

128
00:08:15,824 --> 00:08:17,654
Oww!

129
00:08:19,224 --> 00:08:20,964
Who do you think you are?!

130
00:08:20,964 --> 00:08:22,324
Stop it!

131
00:08:25,164 --> 00:08:26,934
Ms. Sayaka.

132
00:08:29,104 --> 00:08:32,194
I've asked you before not to come
while the kindergarten is open.

133
00:08:32,404 --> 00:08:34,634
You've got the nerve to give us orders.

134
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:37,584
If you had paid your debts, this
wouldn't be happening, would it?

135
00:08:37,584 --> 00:08:39,174
"Teacher."

136
00:08:39,884 --> 00:08:44,784
Just because our boss is a nice man, don't you
be thinking you get special privileges.

137
00:08:46,124 --> 00:08:48,994
I will speak with you after the
kindergarten is closed. So please...

138
00:08:48,994 --> 00:08:53,554
We'll get out of here as soon as you
return what's owed to us. So...

139
00:08:53,724 --> 00:08:56,594
Hurry and pay up!

140
00:08:57,834 --> 00:08:59,264
Well?!

141
00:08:59,264 --> 00:09:00,094
You...

142
00:09:07,674 --> 00:09:09,004
What's she?

143
00:09:14,314 --> 00:09:16,584
P-Please leave!

144
00:09:17,184 --> 00:09:19,314
What the?

145
00:09:19,824 --> 00:09:21,684
K-Kobato...

146
00:09:22,294 --> 00:09:23,784
Please leave!

147
00:09:24,524 --> 00:09:27,824
We don't have time to be playing
games with brats like you!

148
00:09:30,604 --> 00:09:31,994
Please leave!

149
00:09:34,404 --> 00:09:36,094
What is this girl?

150
00:09:36,474 --> 00:09:38,304
Police officer!

151
00:09:38,304 --> 00:09:43,144
Help! There are some scary men
here! Hurry and come!

152
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:46,714
We'll leave you alone today, but we'll
keep coming back until you pay!

153
00:09:46,814 --> 00:09:48,304
Hey, let go of me!

154
00:09:53,324 --> 00:09:55,724
Are you okay, Ms. Sayaka?

155
00:10:00,094 --> 00:10:02,994
Yes, I'm fine.

156
00:10:04,834 --> 00:10:05,894
Toshihiko!

157
00:10:05,964 --> 00:10:07,734
Are you okay?

158
00:10:10,674 --> 00:10:12,364
I was just faking it. I'm fine!

159
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:16,404
I thought they might leave if I said police.

160
00:10:16,714 --> 00:10:20,544
Is that right? And they really did leave.

161
00:10:20,714 --> 00:10:22,084
Good thinking!

162
00:10:22,084 --> 00:10:24,174
Toshihiko, you were great!

163
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,114
That was nothing.

164
00:10:26,384 --> 00:10:28,824
But if they ever come again,
I'll chase them away.

165
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:34,494
For a Dobato, you did a great job.

166
00:10:35,364 --> 00:10:38,854
But how much longer do I have to stay like this?

167
00:10:56,784 --> 00:10:59,444
So yesterday's call was from those guys.

168
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:03,454
Ms. Sayaka seemed troubled.

169
00:11:03,754 --> 00:11:06,724
I wonder if there's anything I can do for her?

170
00:11:06,894 --> 00:11:08,224
You don't have any money.

171
00:11:09,694 --> 00:11:15,164
But maybe, she would feel better if
I were able to pay her debt off.

172
00:11:22,444 --> 00:11:23,434
What is it?

173
00:11:24,484 --> 00:11:26,034
Cashing
OK from 50,000 yen
Special offer campaign!!

174
00:11:29,184 --> 00:11:31,984
Are you out of your mind?!

175
00:11:40,424 --> 00:11:41,654
That guy...

176
00:11:42,034 --> 00:11:45,004
There he is again. What's he doing?

177
00:11:47,574 --> 00:11:50,564
What's this? Could he be?!

178
00:11:51,974 --> 00:11:53,404
Excuse me!

179
00:11:56,014 --> 00:11:58,414
Are you not feeling well?

180
00:11:59,444 --> 00:12:02,004
I'm fine. It's nothing.

181
00:12:02,214 --> 00:12:03,344
Um...

182
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:06,484
Isn't there anything I can do for you?

183
00:12:06,654 --> 00:12:08,854
If something is troubling you...

184
00:12:09,594 --> 00:12:12,114
Nothing is troubling me.

185
00:12:12,394 --> 00:12:16,194
I have a house to go home to.
I just like being here. That's all.

186
00:12:16,294 --> 00:12:18,024
I understand.

187
00:12:20,604 --> 00:12:22,504
That book you had yesterday.

188
00:12:22,704 --> 00:12:25,334
Oh, I borrowed this from the kindergarten.

189
00:12:25,944 --> 00:12:29,394
I'm practicing but I'm not getting
much better at reading it.

190
00:12:29,914 --> 00:12:31,644
I told you not to read it.

191
00:12:31,984 --> 00:12:36,354
Why not? Everybody loves this story.

192
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,984
That's why I want to get good at reading it.

193
00:12:38,984 --> 00:12:40,784
I'm begging you not to read it!

194
00:12:47,964 --> 00:12:49,024
It's nothing.

195
00:12:49,794 --> 00:12:50,994
Forget about it.

196
00:12:55,074 --> 00:12:58,264
Does he really hate this book so much?

197
00:13:06,844 --> 00:13:10,044
What are you doing here?

198
00:13:10,984 --> 00:13:12,484
Because I live here.

199
00:13:12,484 --> 00:13:14,284
You're my next door neighbor?!

200
00:13:15,154 --> 00:13:16,744
Can't you tell?

201
00:13:19,064 --> 00:13:20,324
Um!

202
00:13:20,324 --> 00:13:21,524
What is it?

203
00:13:21,834 --> 00:13:26,264
A guy at the park told me,
"don't read this picture book".

204
00:13:27,304 --> 00:13:28,704
So you met Mr. Mori?

205
00:13:29,174 --> 00:13:30,464
Mr. Mori?

206
00:13:32,504 --> 00:13:34,604
What about Ioryogi-san?

207
00:13:34,674 --> 00:13:37,234
No, I'm talking about the
guy who wrote the book.

208
00:13:37,374 --> 00:13:38,744
Oh...

209
00:13:40,084 --> 00:13:42,054
What?! Really?!

210
00:13:42,254 --> 00:13:44,554
He's actually quite famous around here.

211
00:13:44,554 --> 00:13:49,014
But, but, then why would he tell me
"don't read this picture book"?

212
00:13:49,124 --> 00:13:50,214
I don't know.

213
00:13:51,264 --> 00:13:52,094
But...

214
00:13:52,094 --> 00:13:56,554
I did hear that he hasn't written a book since.

215
00:13:58,664 --> 00:14:00,934
This was his last book?

216
00:14:01,034 --> 00:14:05,944
Firefly's Light

217
00:14:05,944 --> 00:14:10,814
Firefly's Light
Once upon a time there was a firefly, who
lived by the side of a beautiful stream.

218
00:14:10,814 --> 00:14:11,144
Firefly's Light

219
00:14:12,044 --> 00:14:17,044
Firefly had been living all
alone for a long, long time.

220
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:21,484
It had been so long that Firefly had
completely forgotten that he was a firefly.

221
00:14:22,694 --> 00:14:30,564
One dark night, a night when the moon was not
out, Firefly saw a pretty light in the distance.

222
00:14:31,334 --> 00:14:36,064
Wondering what it was, he went
closer and found a girl insect.

223
00:14:37,944 --> 00:14:42,074
"You're very pretty. What kind of an
insect are you?" Firefly asked.

224
00:14:42,374 --> 00:14:48,904
"I'm a firefly, just like you" she answered.

225
00:14:49,614 --> 00:14:51,954
Then she said, "Why don't you
glow like the rest of us?"

226
00:14:52,854 --> 00:14:58,054
Firefly had lived alone for so
long and forgot how to glow.

227
00:14:59,724 --> 00:15:05,564
But seeing the sad expression on Firefly's face,
the little girl firefly taught him how to shine.

228
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:13,394
Ever since, the two spent days and nights
shining together by the riverside.

229
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:21,034
I guess the old man forgot how to shine too.

230
00:15:21,954 --> 00:15:25,354
Who knows for what reason,
but just like the firefly in that book.

231
00:15:26,424 --> 00:15:29,184
Isn't there anything we can do for him?

232
00:15:34,024 --> 00:15:36,154
Nakayoshi Library
(Friendship Library)

233
00:15:36,464 --> 00:15:37,594
Ecology of the Firefly
Japan Firefly Research Center

234
00:15:37,964 --> 00:15:40,124
Hey, now what are you up to?

235
00:15:40,504 --> 00:15:41,804
We're going to find it!

236
00:15:41,804 --> 00:15:42,794
Huh?

237
00:15:46,704 --> 00:15:47,864
Hey!

238
00:15:53,014 --> 00:15:54,814
Are you free tonight?

239
00:16:03,294 --> 00:16:05,264
Come and see the fireflies with me!

240
00:16:05,794 --> 00:16:07,924
I'll be waiting for you in the forest of
Hachiman-yama, by the stream.

241
00:16:18,444 --> 00:16:22,034
Firefly's memory came back. "I'm a firefly."

242
00:16:22,814 --> 00:16:25,674
I can glow, just like you.

243
00:16:26,514 --> 00:16:28,244
You've improved.

244
00:16:28,584 --> 00:16:31,614
I'm sure he'll remember how to glow.

245
00:16:31,854 --> 00:16:34,884
But... There's no sight of him.

246
00:16:37,224 --> 00:16:39,024
You came!

247
00:16:39,664 --> 00:16:41,854
Yeah, not that I really wanted to.

248
00:16:42,434 --> 00:16:46,564
Oh, um... the fireflies...
they haven't shown up yet.

249
00:16:47,104 --> 00:16:49,434
Why... did you say what you did?

250
00:16:50,904 --> 00:16:54,804
"Come and see the fireflies with me. I'll be
waiting at Hachiman-yama, by the stream."

251
00:16:55,844 --> 00:16:58,074
Those were the exact words
that Naoko said to me.

252
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,474
Naoko?

253
00:17:01,684 --> 00:17:04,214
She was my love.

254
00:17:04,214 --> 00:17:05,124
What?

255
00:17:05,124 --> 00:17:06,624
Those pictures.

256
00:17:06,624 --> 00:17:08,714
They're Naoko's drawings.

257
00:17:09,254 --> 00:17:11,564
She suggested a story about
fireflies would be nice,

258
00:17:11,564 --> 00:17:15,794
so I wrote the story and then
she drew the pictures.

259
00:17:17,134 --> 00:17:19,194
Come and see the fireflies with me.

260
00:17:20,704 --> 00:17:23,634
Come, let's go see the fireflies!

261
00:17:24,234 --> 00:17:24,404
Remember? We promised.

262
00:17:24,404 --> 00:17:26,464
Very well. I understand.
Remember? We promised.

263
00:17:27,274 --> 00:17:28,644
I don't have time.

264
00:17:28,644 --> 00:17:30,074
Please don't say that.

265
00:17:30,074 --> 00:17:31,474
I've found the perfect place.

266
00:17:32,344 --> 00:17:34,014
I'm telling you, I don't have time.

267
00:17:34,014 --> 00:17:36,004
I'll be waiting for you at
Hachiman-yama, by the stream.

268
00:17:42,924 --> 00:17:43,424
Hello? Yes. Yes.

269
00:17:43,424 --> 00:17:45,664
As it turned out, I wasn't able to go.
Hello? Yes. Yes.

270
00:17:45,664 --> 00:17:46,454
As it turned out, I wasn't able to go.

271
00:17:47,964 --> 00:17:49,894
Those days, I was always busy.

272
00:17:49,894 --> 00:17:51,864
I had many deadlines to meet.

273
00:17:52,504 --> 00:17:54,734
So your girlfriend went alone.

274
00:17:56,434 --> 00:17:58,374
"They were very beautiful."

275
00:17:58,474 --> 00:18:01,304
"I would've liked for you to see
them, too", she told me.

276
00:18:04,484 --> 00:18:09,214
Naoko's pictures always seemed so
lonely. But they were beautiful.

277
00:18:09,884 --> 00:18:14,084
So that's why I decided to rewrite it
into a sad, yet beautiful story.

278
00:18:14,354 --> 00:18:18,294
Then, some time after the book was completed...

279
00:18:18,964 --> 00:18:20,924
Are you finally getting some time off?

280
00:18:20,924 --> 00:18:23,484
Yeah. I'll meet you at the park.

281
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:41,184
Naoko. Hey, Naoko! Come on!

282
00:18:42,254 --> 00:18:44,314
Sotaro?

283
00:18:44,314 --> 00:18:45,614
Yeah, I'm right here.

284
00:18:46,154 --> 00:18:47,584
Is there anything that you want?

285
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,054
I'll bring you whatever you'd like.

286
00:18:51,064 --> 00:18:52,064
Fireflies...

287
00:18:52,064 --> 00:18:53,424
What?

288
00:18:53,424 --> 00:18:58,094
I wish... we could have seen
the fireflies together.

289
00:19:05,304 --> 00:19:08,144
Why didn't I go with her then?

290
00:19:08,974 --> 00:19:11,034
She wanted so badly to see them with me.

291
00:19:12,144 --> 00:19:13,074
And yet I...

292
00:19:13,984 --> 00:19:15,414
Why?

293
00:19:21,724 --> 00:19:22,954
Let's go home.

294
00:19:23,494 --> 00:19:25,484
P-Please wait!

295
00:19:26,364 --> 00:19:27,794
Just a bit longer!

296
00:19:27,794 --> 00:19:29,734
Just wait a bit longer and I'm sure...

297
00:19:39,674 --> 00:19:40,704
Are you all right?

298
00:19:40,704 --> 00:19:42,374
I-I'm sorry.

299
00:19:53,124 --> 00:19:54,314
This place...

300
00:20:03,364 --> 00:20:06,894
Naoko was standing right
here when she drew this.

301
00:20:11,004 --> 00:20:13,034
Right here.

302
00:20:33,764 --> 00:20:35,124
Fireflies...

303
00:20:47,304 --> 00:20:49,434
Huh? You've never seen fireflies before?

304
00:20:49,744 --> 00:20:51,574
So what? Anything wrong with that?

305
00:20:51,714 --> 00:20:53,684
Then, come see them with me.

306
00:20:53,884 --> 00:20:55,874
You've got to see them for yourself.

307
00:20:56,314 --> 00:20:58,914
You won't find fireflies near here these days.

308
00:20:59,724 --> 00:21:02,624
I'll show them to you. That's a promise.

309
00:21:14,874 --> 00:21:16,804
It was a promise...

310
00:21:24,274 --> 00:21:25,764
Wow!

311
00:21:27,114 --> 00:21:28,374
They're pretty.

312
00:21:28,514 --> 00:21:29,414
The fireflies.

313
00:21:42,294 --> 00:21:45,064
They really are beautiful.

314
00:21:46,964 --> 00:21:48,404
Yes.

315
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:57,274
Looks like the man's remembered how to glow.

316
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,844
He's started writing his next book, right?

317
00:22:07,224 --> 00:22:10,784
And to prove that take a look at this.

318
00:22:12,224 --> 00:22:13,754
There's more!

319
00:22:14,524 --> 00:22:16,034
So what that means is...

320
00:22:16,034 --> 00:22:18,464
That man was comforted.

321
00:22:19,334 --> 00:22:23,234
So I was helpful to him.

322
00:22:24,304 --> 00:22:28,744
So this time, I would like to give you
the entire one hundred points, but...

323
00:22:29,374 --> 00:22:32,674
I am going to take away points for the
way you treated me at the library...

324
00:22:35,184 --> 00:22:37,044
Kobato, eighty points!

325
00:22:37,584 --> 00:22:40,314
Wow! Thank you so very much!

326
00:22:40,454 --> 00:22:42,754
Don't lighten up. We're picking up the pace now!

327
00:22:43,294 --> 00:22:45,784
Yes sir! Kobato is ready!

328
00:22:46,624 --> 00:22:50,594
But then again, given the treatment you
gave me, eighty's a bit too generous.

329
00:22:50,594 --> 00:22:51,534
Fifty's more like it.

330
00:22:51,534 --> 00:22:54,404
No, no way! I much prefer 80.

331
00:22:54,404 --> 00:22:55,534
Then, in that case...

332
00:22:55,534 --> 00:22:56,404
Yes sir!

333
00:22:56,404 --> 00:22:57,134
79 points.

334
00:22:57,134 --> 00:22:57,874
What?! How'd you come up with that?!
79 points.

335
00:22:57,874 --> 00:22:59,864
What?! How'd you come up with that?!

336
00:23:01,274 --> 00:23:08,914
Everyone dreams of flying

337
00:23:10,084 --> 00:23:16,184
But they let gravity trick them

338
00:23:16,454 --> 00:23:24,294
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

339
00:23:26,534 --> 00:23:32,874
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

340
00:23:33,904 --> 00:23:36,774
Is because he

341
00:23:36,774 --> 00:23:43,914
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

342
00:23:44,084 --> 00:23:46,614
In that case

343
00:23:46,784 --> 00:23:50,894
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

344
00:23:50,894 --> 00:23:54,764
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

345
00:23:54,764 --> 00:24:02,104
That exchange would fill you with joy

346
00:24:02,634 --> 00:24:06,864
It would make you feel so happy

347
00:24:07,174 --> 00:24:11,414
There's nothing to worry about

348
00:24:11,414 --> 00:24:15,504
Since we're together

349
00:24:17,284 --> 00:24:23,224
It's strange how I'm crying

350
00:24:23,224 --> 00:24:26,094
Even though I'm happy

351
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:28,964
Next episode
...Hide and Seek.
Even though I'm happy

352
00:24:28,964 --> 00:24:30,794
Next episode
...Hide and Seek.

